// The elemental matter and fire sprites: gases, liquids and solids that
// lie on the floor, and fire. Authored by `tools/art/elemental/`; the art
// rules are docs/art-reference/elemental-asset-guide.md.
//
// A `single` is one 32x32 picture, tagged `idle` (one frame is a still,
// more frames loop). A `smooth strip` is 160x32, five blocks side by side
// (0 convex, 1 vertical, 2 horizontal, 3 concave, 4 flat), tagged `idle-s`
// so `Slice(5, 1, ...)` can cut it: `<name>_0_0` .. `<name>_0_4`, block
// `c` playing every frame of the tag. The client picks each 16x16 quarter
// of a tile from the block its two sides and corner select.
//
// Gas, liquid and solid sprites are neutral greys the substance's own tint
// multiplies at draw time, so no tint is declared here. Fire sprites carry
// their own colours except the two `tintable` ones, which are grey too.
(
    sheets: [
        ("gas_cloud_smooth_gentle", "art/matter/gasses/gas_cloud_smooth_gentle.aseprite"),
        ("gas_cloud_smooth_still", "art/matter/gasses/gas_cloud_smooth_still.aseprite"),
        ("gas_cloud_smooth_stirred", "art/matter/gasses/gas_cloud_smooth_stirred.aseprite"),
        ("gas_mist_smooth_gentle", "art/matter/gasses/gas_mist_smooth_gentle.aseprite"),
